/guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T18:10:01+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133241198,imgsize-949222.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Pakistani minister in Balochistan province escapes armed attack on convoy]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133241418.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[.The attack took place in the Khad Kocha area as Langove was travelling from Quetta to Kalat, Balochistan government spokesperson Shahid Rind said. "Six people were injured in the attack, but the minister remained unhurt and the convoy has returned to Quetta," Rind said. All six injured people suffered bullet wounds, according to a senior police official. Three of them were police personnel, with two reportedly in serious condition.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/pakistan/pakistani-minister-in-balochistan-province-escapes-armed-attack-on-convoy/articleshow/133241418.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/pakistan/pakistani-minister-in-balochistan-province-escapes-armed-attack-on-convoy/articleshow/133241418.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T17:58:34+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133241469,imgsize-1750713.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Volhynia massacres: Russia using WWII to plant discord between Ukraine and Poland?]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133239283.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The historical dispute centres on the Volhynia massacres between 1943 and 1945. Poland says Ukrainian nationalists killed around 100,000 Poles during the violence, while thousands of Ukrainians were also killed in retaliatory attacks. Tensions over the issue increased after Ukrainian President Volodymyr Zelenskyy named an army unit after insurgents linked to the massacres. Polish president Karol Nawrocki responded by stripping Zelenskyy of a major Polish honour in June.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/volhynia-massacres-russia-using-wwii-to-plant-discord-between-ukraine-and-poland/articleshow/133239283.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/volhynia-massacres-russia-using-wwii-to-plant-discord-between-ukraine-and-poland/articleshow/133239283.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T16:54:32+05:30</pubDate><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133239724,imgsize-295332.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[London river was declared 'biologically dead' in 1957; decades later it is filled with sharks and seals]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133238994.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The River Thames in London has made a remarkable recovery, evolving from a biologically barren stretch to a vibrant ecosystem full of life, such as sharks and seals. This revitalization is attributed to decades of pollution management and enhanced sewage systems. The Thames Tideway Tunnel plays a crucial role in minimizing sewage discharge. However, challenges like warming waters and nitrate pollution still pose threats.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/london-river-was-declared-biologically-dead-in-1957-decades-later-it-is-filled-with-sharks-and-seals/articleshow/133238994.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/london-river-was-declared-biologically-dead-in-1957-decades-later-it-is-filled-with-sharks-and-seals/articleshow/133238994.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T17:56:37+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133239074,imgsize-129284.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[UK heatwaves help bananas fruit, experts explain why it’s unusual]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133236922.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/bananas-are-fruiting-in-uk-gardens-after-heatwaves-why-experts-say-this-is-unusual/articleshow/133236922.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/bananas-are-fruiting-in-uk-gardens-after-heatwaves-why-experts-say-this-is-unusual/articleshow/133236922.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T17:55:52+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133237459,imgsize-186088.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Ryanair passenger partially sucked through airplane window after engine blade smashed into cabin: Report]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133240396.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/ryanair-passenger-partially-sucked-through-airplane-window-after-engine-blade-smashed-into-cabin-report/articleshow/133240396.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/ryanair-passenger-partially-sucked-through-airplane-window-after-engine-blade-smashed-into-cabin-report/articleshow/133240396.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T17:42:21+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">Gokul Ankari</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133240790,imgsize-624440.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Nigel Farage beats ‘space warrior trashcan’ rival in UK by-poll he triggered]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133240633.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Nigel Farage claimed a decisive win in the Clacton parliamentary by-election, following his resignation amid controversies surrounding his financial dealings. His nearest rival, the comedic character Count Binface, surprisingly garnered a considerable share of support. Meanwhile, prominent parties in Westminster chose to abstain from the election, deeming it a mere political ploy. This by-election stemmed from Farage's prior resignation and his ambition to retake his seat.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/nigel-farage-beats-space-warrior-trashcan-rival-in-uk-by-poll-he-triggered/articleshow/133240633.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/nigel-farage-beats-space-warrior-trashcan-rival-in-uk-by-poll-he-triggered/articleshow/133240633.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T17:36:46+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133241061,imgsize-116568.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Bernie Marcus' foundation gives $28.7M for heart-repair stem cell research]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133240183.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/home-depot-billionaire-bernie-marcus-foundation-donates-28-7-million-to-stem-cell-research-that-could-repair-hearts-damaged-by-heart-attacks/articleshow/133240183.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/home-depot-billionaire-bernie-marcus-foundation-donates-28-7-million-to-stem-cell-research-that-could-repair-hearts-damaged-by-heart-attacks/articleshow/133240183.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T17:26:10+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133240539,imgsize-1238369.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[7,000-year-old ‘Stargazer’ statuette from ancient Turkey raises mysteries]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133239973.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[A 5,000-year-old marble statuette called "The Stargazer" originates from ancient Turkey. This rare figure, dating to 3000 BCE, is remarkably whole and unbroken. Its oversized head and upward gaze create a distinctive, stylized human form. The statuette's original purpose remains a mystery due to its ancient origins. Similar figures have been found across Western Anatolia and nearby regions.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/5000-year-old-stargazer-statuette-from-ancient-turkey-reveals-a-mysterious-early-human-sculpture/articleshow/133239973.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/5000-year-old-stargazer-statuette-from-ancient-turkey-reveals-a-mysterious-early-human-sculpture/articleshow/133239973.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T17:21:05+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133240226,imgsize-32539.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Quote of the day by Martin Luther King Jr: 'There is some good in the worst of us and some evil in the best of us. When we discover this, we are less prone to hate our enemies']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133239755.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Martin Luther King Jr. eloquently illustrates the dual nature of humanity and our collective imperfections. By acknowledging our flaws, we foster empathy, which diminishes hostility and paves the way for productive conflict resolution. This understanding of shared vulnerabilities encourages dialogue and reconciliation, transforming resentment into compassion and commitment to understanding one another.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/quote-of-the-day-by-martin-luther-king-jr-there-is-some-good-in-the-worst-of-us-and-some-evil-in-the-best-of-us-when-we-discover-this-we-are-less-prone-to-hate-our-enemies/articleshow/133239755.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/quote-of-the-day-by-martin-luther-king-jr-there-is-some-good-in-the-worst-of-us-and-some-evil-in-the-best-of-us-when-we-discover-this-we-are-less-prone-to-hate-our-enemies/articleshow/133239755.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T16:59:44+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133239824,imgsize-86704.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Massachusetts residents sue data centre over 27 diesel generators near homes]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133239275.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/massachusetts-residents-sue-data-centre-over-27-diesel-generators-and-16-cooling-towers-near-homes-raising-fears-of-pollution-and-noise/articleshow/133239275.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/massachusetts-residents-sue-data-centre-over-27-diesel-generators-and-16-cooling-towers-near-homes-raising-fears-of-pollution-and-noise/articleshow/133239275.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T16:57:07+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133239754,imgsize-1630200.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Why has Britain's grass turned yellow? Scientists warn about the future of the island after 'driest month ever']]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133238537.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[After experiencing the driest July on record, England's picturesque green fields have succumbed to a fading yellow hue. This alarming trend of increasing heatwaves significantly affects lawns and public parks. While native grasses possess resilience during droughts and can deepen their roots to conserve water, extended dry periods inevitably lead them to enter a dormant state, awaiting rain.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/why-has-britains-grass-turned-yellow-scientists-warn-about-the-future-of-the-island-after-driest-month-ever/articleshow/133238537.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/science/why-has-britains-grass-turned-yellow-scientists-warn-about-the-future-of-the-island-after-driest-month-ever/articleshow/133238537.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T16:18:29+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI Science Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133238585,imgsize-229421.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Nearly 80 men found shackled in an ancient Athens mass grave were locals]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133238216.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/nearly-80-men-found-shackled-in-an-ancient-athens-mass-grave-were-locals-not-outsiders/articleshow/133238216.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/europe/nearly-80-men-found-shackled-in-an-ancient-athens-mass-grave-were-locals-not-outsiders/articleshow/133238216.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T16:11:43+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133238361,imgsize-140280.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[18-year-old turns back 400m from Everest summit, returns a year later to make history]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133236766.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/meet-bianca-adler-the-18-year-old-from-melbourne-who-turned-back-400-metres-from-everests-summit-then-returned-a-year-later-and-made-history/articleshow/133236766.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/rest-of-world/meet-bianca-adler-the-18-year-old-from-melbourne-who-turned-back-400-metres-from-everests-summit-then-returned-a-year-later-and-made-history/articleshow/133236766.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T15:56:18+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133236869,imgsize-147608.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Surrogacy dispute escalates after McKenna West gives birth to baby with heart defect]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133236619.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[The surrogacy dispute escalated significantly when McKenna West delivered a newborn with a critical heart condition. This infant is currently under the care of intended parents Nausheen Gilkar and Omar Ahmed. Meanwhile, West is fighting against the custody agreements and claims over parental rights in Texas, where the intricate web of contrasting state laws complicates the situation, leading to ongoing legal battles as all parties await further judicial rulings.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-multi-state-surrogacy-dispute-escalated-after-mckenna-west-gave-birth-in-texas-to-a-baby-with-a-severe-heart-defect-the-intended-parents-now-have-custody-while-the-legal-fight-continues/articleshow/133236619.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/a-multi-state-surrogacy-dispute-escalated-after-mckenna-west-gave-birth-in-texas-to-a-baby-with-a-severe-heart-defect-the-intended-parents-now-have-custody-while-the-legal-fight-continues/articleshow/133236619.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T15:31:54+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133236794,imgsize-64311.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Indian-origin man rejected for H-1B three times, spent $13,000 and formed 700 pages of evidence to stay in US]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133232380.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[Sohan Sethi faced multiple H-1B visa rejections after arriving in the United States. He then pursued an O-1 visa, requiring extensive documentation and lawyer fees. Sethi demonstrated extraordinary ability through achievements and industry recognition to secure his stay. This path highlights the challenges faced by skilled professionals seeking to remain in America. He now manages a team, sharing his experience to guide others through the process.]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-origin-man-rejected-for-h-1b-visa-three-times-compiled-700-pages-of-evidence-and-spent-13000-to-secure-another-way-to-stay-in-us/articleshow/133232380.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/us/indian-origin-man-rejected-for-h-1b-visa-three-times-compiled-700-pages-of-evidence-and-spent-13000-to-secure-another-way-to-stay-in-us/articleshow/133232380.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T14:00:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133232553,imgsize-94659.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Couple renovating their farmhouse kitchen found more than 1,000 coins buried]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133231178.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-dorset-couple-renovating-their-farmhouse-kitchen-found-more-than-1000-coins-buried-since-englands-civil-war/articleshow/133231178.cms]]></link><guid><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/world/uk/a-dorset-couple-renovating-their-farmhouse-kitchen-found-more-than-1000-coins-buried-since-englands-civil-war/articleshow/133231178.cms]]></guid><pubDate>2026-08-14T12:30:00+05:30</pubDate><dc:creator xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/">TOI World Desk</dc:creator><enclosure type="image/jpeg" url="https://static.toiimg.com/photo/msid-133231432,imgsize-130656.cms"/></item><item><title><![CDATA[Australia’s feral camels roamed free for decades. Now Gulf breeders want them]]></title><description>&lt;img border="0" hspace="10" align="left" style="margin-top:3px;margin-right:5px;" src="https://timesofindia.indiatimes.com/photo/133232150.cms" /&gt;<![CDATA[]]></description><link><![CDATA[https://timesofindia.